    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2RiZDVd8Fb6BcQM4DoVrfQ5)_\n\n## Summary\nThe top-level `* Provide` section of 84 literate docs in `.config/emacs-modular/docs/tangles/` is now a one-line summary and a single source block holding the whole `;;; Provide` segment. Before, each had a sub-heading per form (for example \"Provide marker\", \"Provide form\") with its own prose and block. Property drawers are kept.\n\n## Verification\nI tangled every doc before and after the change with Emacs (org-babel-tangle-file). The tangled `.el` files under `libraries/modules/` are identical.\n\n## Not changed\nAbout 35 docs have a provide subsection inside a topical section (for example \"Keybindings and provide\"). I left those alone, since the request was about the `Provide` heading.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01ACbiw1tHxZUgAEj5duertR)_",
